---
title: Rajma
description: Red kidney bean curry with lots of fresh ginger and canned tomato sauce, simmered in 20 minutes.
tags: [curry, year-round]
course: main
icons: [pepper-hot, garlic, bowl-hot]
cuisine: Indian
source:
  name: Smitten Kitchen
  url: https://smittenkitchen.com/2009/02/red-kidney-bean-curry/
adapted: true
servings: 6
prep time: 15m
cook time: 20m
---

Heat the @extra-virgin olive oil{1/3%cup}(we use less) in a deep #saucepan{} over medium heat for ~heat{1%minute}.

Add the @fresh ginger{2%tbsp}(minced, reduced from the original 4 tbsp), @garlic cloves{3}(chopped), @onion{1}(medium, finely chopped), and @?green chile{1}(large, chopped), and let sizzle for ~sizzle{1%minute}.

Add the @tomato sauce{1%can}(8 oz, or 1 cup of one of your choice), @salt{1/2%tsp}(reduced by half from the original), and the remaining spices: @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, @cumin seeds{1/2%tsp}, @ground turmeric{1/2%tsp}, and @cayenne{1/8%tsp}(reduced by half from the original). Cook for an additional ~cook{5%minutes}, stirring frequently.

Add the @red kidney beans{3%cup}(cooked, or 2 15-oz cans, drained and rinsed) plus @water{2%cup} and the @plum tomato{1}(diced).

Bring to a boil, then reduce to medium heat and cook uncovered for ~simmer{10%minutes}. Remove from the heat.

Garnish with the @fresh cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped, or parsley if you're cilantro-averse).

> Serve over rice or with naan. A dollop of plain yogurt (if not keeping the dish vegan) on top is heavenly.
